# A VARIANT, NEVER THE PRODUCT: THE GHOST BEHIND THE CAR, FOR THE WHOLE PICTURE, BY THE LIGHT THAT STAYS AT A SCREEN PLACE
# (THE TEXT OF 2026-10-12: docs\reports\fg-3\sitting-2026-10-12\BRIEF-lib4.md, and lib4\README.md beside it for its
# numbers. The text the owner ran in the game that morning is v-env-1.cut; the form's own story is in
# docs\reports\fg-3\desk-2026-10-11-ghost.) IT CHANGES THE PICTURE. Built only into a variant library
# (build-ffx-own.ps1 -Variant; tools\ffx-own\build_variants.py env, and ship), FROM THE PRODUCT.
#
# WHAT AMD'S CODE DOES THERE. The interpolation knows one motion a pixel, the ground's. The car's shadow, glow, shading
# and reflection lie on that ground and stay with the car on the screen. So a fetched piece of ground arrives with the
# light of the place it was fetched from: a band of sunlit ground under the car, a second outline behind it.
#
# THE VARIANT, in two passes of AMD's and with no pass added:
#   OPTICAL FLOW'S FIRST PASS (it makes the brightness optical flow searches in: one thread for two by two pixels of the
#     picture, and it loads their four colours for its own work) also writes THE TWO ENVELOPES of the real frame, AT
#     THE SAME SCREEN PLACE frame after frame, of three numbers: the log of the brightness (one texel for two by two
#     pixels, the mean of those pixels: the down-sampling is the blur), and THE TINT, the log of red over brightness
#     and of blue over brightness (one texel for four by four):
#         up = max(l, up_before - step)        lo = min(l, lo_before + step)
#     step is ENV_STEP of the log a real frame of 16.7 ms (it follows the frame time), OR ENV_SHARE OF WHAT IS LEFT TO
#     GO where that is less (with the plain step a texture whose own contrast is under the step is never forgotten).
#     Light that stays at a place is in both; a shadow that streams past with the ground is forgotten by `up`, a
#     passing pool of light by `lo`.
#     (WHY THIS PASS. v-env-1 wrote them in the disocclusion mask's pass, by a filtered tap of the picture a texel: that
#     pass then read the whole picture, 63 MiB, for nothing else, and it was most of what the writing cost. Here the
#     four colours are in hand. The picture is the same one: optical flow is handed the HUD-less image where one is
#     bound, as the interpolation is.)
#     Two images a pair (two channels of brightness, four of tint), made by the glue on the shared backend because two
#     of AMD's effects use them (ffx-own\glue\dlssiv_fg.cpp, DLSSIV_FG_CUT_ENV); the frame before's are the ones the
#     call before wrote (they change places at every optical flow call). The dispatch of a reset, and the first of
#     all, writes the frame itself into both and reads nothing.
#   THE INTERPOLATION PASS, for the two colours fetched along the game's vector, each with its fetch place f and the
#     place p it is put, and for each of the three numbers: g_up = up(p) - up(f), g_lo = lo(p) - lo(f); the gain
#     needed is the smaller of the two in size where they agree in sign and 0 where they do not (the brightness's held
#     within log 1/16 and log 16, a tint's within ENV_TINT_MOST).
#     THE DEAD BAND IS NOT ONE NUMBER: a gain is believed only as far as it stands out of what the place and the fetch
#     place have themselves been seen to vary by, the gap between their two envelopes (the larger of the two gaps,
#     and ENV_GATE_WIDTH more): nothing under ENV_GATE_0 times that, whole from ENV_GATE_1 times that on. Where
#     nothing is believed the pixel takes THE PRODUCT'S PATH EXACTLY: no colour and no weight is touched.
#     Else each sample's red, green and blue are multiplied by exp(the brightness's gain and the tints' in it), and
#     where two samples are blended each one's share is multiplied by exp(-|what it needed| / ENV_TRUST): the sample
#     that needed the least relighting is believed.
#     THE TINT RIDES ON THE BRIGHTNESS: its image is fetched only where a sample's brightness is believed (more than
#     ENV_LEAST); a difference of colour alone, with no difference of brightness to carry it, is left to the product.
#     NO FLARE: a relit sample is never brighter than ENV_OVER times the brightest the place itself has been seen, unless
#     it was so before it was relit.
#     Nothing is done in the dispatch of a reset (AMD's pass copies the real frame there) nor in the ENV_FRAME_0 frames
#     after it; whole from ENV_FRAME_1 frames after it on. Nothing is done where the game's vector is zero.
#   The two colours fetched along optical flow's own vector are left as they are (where that vector is the game's
#     they are the game's two, relit).
#
# THE THREE MENDS OF 2026-10-12, each one marked block of the text below (v-env-less-creep.cut, v-env-less-apart.cut and
# v-env-less-moved.cut take one out each, to judge and to price it by itself). WHAT WAS LEFT in the game, "near where
# the back bumper and the tyre meet, projected onto the road", is THE CAR'S OWN SHADOW WHERE IT HAS JUST ARRIVED: the car
# shifts on the screen a pixel or two a frame, its shadow and its outline with it, and at a place the shadow reached
# a few frames ago the upper envelope is still on its way down from the sunlight (a quarter of the log a frame: a
# dozen frames for a hard shadow), so the ground put there was relit by a part of what it needed, or by nothing.
#   MEND 1, THE BANDS APART (the interpolation). A gain is also believed where everything the place has been seen to
#     hold lies on one side of everything the fetch place has, however wide the place's own band is.
#   MEND 2, NOTHING FOR A SAMPLE THAT HARDLY MOVES (the interpolation). A thing that stands nearly still on the screen
#     carries its own edges and shading with it; the envelopes' slope across them is not a light it moves through.
#   MEND 3, THE ENVELOPES CREEP (the writing; the one that takes what was left away). Where the frame lies under the
#     upper envelope, that envelope may not stay more than ENV_CREEP_SLACK above the lowest one ENV_CREEP texels away:
#     what has sunk next door has sunk here. A shadow that creeps takes its envelope along (up to 4 pixels a frame);
#     one that streams past with the ground outruns it. The same for the lower envelope and light that creeps.
#
# A PICTURE OF sRGB VALUES (no HDR): the envelopes hold 2.2 times the logs of the raw values, and a gain is taken to the
# power 1 / 2.2 for the raw colour. NOT RUN: every captured run is HDR (scRGB).
#
# NO NEW KIND OF CALL (Linux: plain Direct3D 12 that vkd3d-proton has): loads of a texture by its texel (the picture's
# colours, which the pass loads already; the envelopes of the frame before), filtered samples of one level
# (SampleLevel through AMD's own linear, clamped sampler), stores into float images of two and four channels through
# unordered access views that are never read through them (R16G16_FLOAT and R16G16B16A16_FLOAT, both formats AMD's own
# passes already write so), one constant more in optical flow's constant buffer, log, exp, smoothstep, min, max,
# clamp, dot; the four images are made, handed over and put back in their state by AMD's own backend calls, as its
# optical flow vectors are. No gather, no wave operation, no atomic, no typed load from an unordered access view.
what A VARIANT (the picture changes): each sample of the interpolation is relit for the place it is put, by two envelopes of the real frames' log brightness and tint kept at the screen place, where that stands out of what the two places have been seen to vary by
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_pass, ffx_opticalflow_compute_luminance_pyramid_pass, ffx_opticalflow_compute_optical_flow_advanced_pass_v5, ffx_opticalflow_compute_scd_divergence_pass, ffx_opticalflow_filter_optical_flow_pass_v5, ffx_opticalflow_generate_scd_histogram_pass, ffx_opticalflow_prepare_luma_pass, ffx_opticalflow_scale_optical_flow_advanced_pass_v5
wave64 the same edits in both variants: no wave operation; not run here on a wave64 device
define DLSSIV_FG_CUT_ENV
